  "source_shape_findings": [
    "Road short facade -X and garden long facade -Y meet at the same corner as the 1966 image. These are source-relative coordinates, not compass claims. Indoor stair-end alignment remains unregistered and is not modeled.",
    "Upper 1F/2F share a rectangle; the two emergency raster aspect ratios are not used to invent upper-floor setback/overhang. Historical 1980s building roof y223–228 and column foot y342–347, width approximately x414–680, support about 2.1–2.3 projected garden width/whole-height. v1 40-unit width was reduced to 28 while road width22 and height12.8 remain approximate.",
    "Garden has four broad window bays on each of two upper rows, five outer piers and recessed B1 mirror wall. Real open space between piers and backing is present, not entire B1 through-void and not a filled front wall. Modern PDF fenestration is used instead of recreating the older historical grid.",
    "Road high window narrowed to2.8 and entry widths multiplied by.78, consistent with source photos; these ratios are not precise measured dimensions. Entry canopy, supporting piers and real steps remain; unrelated campus garden/tennis court/long walkways are excluded.",
    "Final roof edge proud0.04 and pier front proud0.08 design units preserve actual material boundaries. All five final views and four comparisons show no former slanted white roof patch on the warm garden wall; independent full-face check finds zero white triangles on that original wall plane.",
    "No RF/as-built section was supplied. Roof is an explicit simple flat closure; visible circular equipment remains a coarse circular silhouette, not an extra occupied storey. Unknown rear/remote fenestration is neutral, not copied from the visible facade. Glass/mirror materials are opaque surface proxies, not optical measurements."
  ],
